WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.700
A rat hears a tone that once came before a mild shock.

2
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.440
It freezes, and its blood pressure rises.

3
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.060
Does one pathway carry both responses?

4
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.080
Neither response is the feeling of fear, but both can be measured.

5
00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:18.833
First, is the response learned?

6
00:00:19.493 --> 00:00:21.753
One group of rats hears tones that predict shocks.

7
00:00:22.793 --> 00:00:26.513
Controls hear the same tones and shocks, kept apart, so the difference estimates

8
00:00:26.513 --> 00:00:32.093
learning. In invented numbers, paired rats froze for 60% % of the tone, and unpaired

9
00:00:32.093 --> 00:00:35.073
rats for 8, a learned difference of 52 points.

10
00:00:36.093 --> 00:00:41.693
Pressure rose 20 mmHg in paired rats, and 3 in unpaired rats, a learned difference

11
00:00:41.693 --> 00:00:42.693
of 17.

12
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:47.403
In a simplified rat circuit, the tone reaches the lateral amygdala.

13
00:00:48.143 --> 00:00:50.623
The central amygdala then sends outputs onward.

14
00:00:51.243 --> 00:00:53.863
One route runs through the lateral hypothalamus.

15
00:00:54.443 --> 00:00:59.243
Another runs through the caudal periaqueductal gray, the sheath of neurons around

16
00:00:59.243 --> 00:01:00.643
the midbrain's fluid canal.

17
00:01:01.343 --> 00:01:02.943
Which route carries which response?

18
00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:08.593
Now cut one route, and ask how much of what was learned is left, after taking away

19
00:01:08.593 --> 00:01:09.793
the unpaired baseline.

20
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:15.973
Lesion the lateral hypothalamus: freezing keeps 94%, percent, but the pressure rise

21
00:01:15.973 --> 00:01:21.353
keeps only 6. Lesion the caudal periaqueductal gray, and it reverses.

22
00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:24.593
Freezing keeps 2%, percent, and pressure keeps 94.

23
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:30.997
Lesion the central amygdala, and both responses fall to about zero, as a shared

24
00:01:30.997 --> 00:01:32.477
source for the two routes predicts.

25
00:01:33.357 --> 00:01:36.517
Each output lesion removed one response and kept the other.

26
00:01:37.077 --> 00:01:41.617
That is a double dissociation: two separate routes below one amygdala node.

27
00:01:42.137 --> 00:01:44.577
It locates the outputs of a defensive response.

28
00:01:44.577 --> 00:01:46.797
It says nothing yet about a feeling.

29
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.880
Patient SM has damage to both amygdalae, and reported at most minimal fear to the

30
00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.080
external threats tested.

31
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.680
Yet she and two other women with that damage all panicked after one breath of 35%

32
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.040
percent CO2. Three of twelve comparison women did.

33
00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:05.680
The kind of threat seems to matter, though the tests also differed.

34
00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.920
Rat work can find necessary steps for a measured response, under defined conditions.

35
00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.920
It cannot say what the animal feels, or that a human feeling takes the same route.
